ion as 'q L_+ - q^{-1} L_- = (q - q^{-1}) L_0'. AGENTS.md 7a fixes the repo convention as L_+ - L_- = (q - q^{-1}) L_0, derived there from the Hecke relation sigma^2 = (q - q^{-1}) sigma + 1 by multiplying through by sigma^{-1} to get sigma - sigma^{-1} = q - q^{-1}, then sending sigma to L_+, sigma^{-1} to L_-, and 1 to L_0. The block's extra q and q^{-1} prefactors are the HOMFLY normalisation (a L_+ - a^{-1} L_- = z L_0), a different relation. reidemeister-mass-invariance.md in this same batch writes the CORRECT form, so the two blocks disagree. PROPOSED: L_+ - L_- = (q - q^{-1}) L_0.","history":2},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:f01","history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:f01","history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"trap","result":"fail","severity":"minor","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:f01","notes":"Thurston's trichotomy is torus / SATELLITE / hyperbolic, and the vanishing-simplicial-volume class is the graph-manifold class: torus knots, the unknot, AND their connected sums and iterated cables. The granny knot 3_1 # 3_1 has zero volume and is not a torus knot (torus knots are prime); nor are cables of torus knots. PROPOSED: 'these are the knots whose complements are graph manifolds — the torus knots, the unknot, and their connected sums and iterated cables'. SECOND ITEM: the fermion dictionary 'the unknot (neutrino), trefoil 3_1 (electron), cinquefoil 5_1 (tau), and the torus(p,2) family' SKIPS THE MUON, the framework's own CAL-2 proxy. That may be deliberate, since the muon is tied to the hyperbolic figure-eight 4_1 (Vol = 2.0299, not zero) and so is not a zero-volume fundamental — but then the list should say so rather than leave a gap between the electron and the tau. THIRD ITEM: the closing paragraph duplicates verbatim the corollary already given in skein-mass-from-linking-proof.md.","history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:f01","history":2},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:f01","history":2},{"id":"uses-editorial-hygiene","group":"uses","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-15","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","history":1},{"id":"uses-formal-coverage","group":"uses","result":"n/a","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-15","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","notes":"block has no .lean sibling","history":1},{"id":"voice-agent-speak","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-15","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-extended.ts","history":1},{"id":"voice-ai-slop","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-15","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-voice.ts","history":2},{"id":"voice-author-notes-pollution","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-15","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-extended.ts","history":1},{"id":"voice-branch-jargon","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"unknown","changed":["md: on disk, no hash recorded","ts: on disk, no hash recorded"],"at":"2026-08-08","reviewer":"agent","by":"local/one-voice-audit","notes":"[EXPIRED-NO-FIELD-HASH] No branch/audit working labels, bean ids, PR/branch references, audit-doc pointers, or agent work-narration found in the .md body or